# Cloudflare Pages redirects — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# This file handles client-side routing for the SPA. Cloudflare Pages
# processes rules top-to-bottom, and static assets (HTML, JS, CSS,
# images) are always served first — `_redirects` only kicks in when no
# static file matches the request path.
#
# Rules:
#   1. /api/* — handled by functions/api/[[path]].ts (Pages Function),
#      NOT by this file. The Pages Function takes precedence over
#      _redirects for /api/* paths.
#   2. /sitemap.xml — handled by functions/sitemap.xml.ts (Pages Function).
#   3. /products/:id — handled by functions/products/[id].ts (Pages Function)
#      for bot detection + OG meta tag injection. Human browsers fall
#      through to the SPA fallback.
#   4. /blog/:slug — handled by functions/blog/[slug].ts (same pattern).
#   5. Everything else — serve index.html so wouter (client-side router)
#      can handle the route. Status 200 (not 302) so the URL in the
#      address bar stays the same.

# SPA fallback — all non-static, non-function routes serve index.html.
/*    /index.html    200
